(Cultural Significance & Notes:) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  Traditional agricultural chant sung at the culmination of rice) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  transplantation during Mangkhap Phanit, expressing thanksgiving for) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(  communal labor.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 11 Tf
(Lyrics & Stanzas \(Tangkhul & English Translation\):) Tj
0 -15 Td
/F2 10 Tf
(  [Stanza 1]) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(    Tangkhul Verses:) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Mangkhap phanitli luisak kashung,") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Phungcham terrace luisang kachung.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Khamathat otli ngasoda pamhaida,") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Aja phanitli ringphapamei.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(    English Gloss:) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "At the arrival of Mangkhap festival, the arduous transplantation is fulfilled,") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Across all the terraced emerald paddies of Phungcham.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Having labored together shoulder to shoulder under monsoon rain,") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Today our community rejoices in hard-won rest and peace.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 10 Tf
(  [Stanza 2]) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(    Tangkhul Verses:) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Avava apuipui wui ngashan kasak,") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Luimahon kazingli chitharan kakhanang.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Aruishon lui won kapha thotta,") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Shim kachivali mashak khare.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(    English Gloss:) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Honoring the sacred agrarian traditions of our fathers and mothers,") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Through weeks of knee-deep mud and relentless toil.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Now the young rice shoots stand vibrant across the fields,") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "And every household prepares the celebratory feast of thanksgiving.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 10 Tf
(  [Stanza 3]) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(    Tangkhul Verses:) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Varewui kakhon kaphali shitsangda,") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Maha thot kaphana ngaraichangra.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Pha-ngayir luili tara kashung,") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Mangkhap wui ringpha mazaingasot.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(    English Gloss:) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "Trusting in the benevolent provision of the Almighty,") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "We look forward with hope to the golden harvest of autumn.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "With mountain waters brimming through irrigation channels,") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(      "We share the cups of fellowship and festival joy.") Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
